text:
Q: Allowing playwright project-scoped setup/teardown tests to be excluded from reports and test counts A: <p>Reporter is not a valid TestProject option per the current docs, it only exists on the top level TestConfig, so setting it inside a project block just gets ignored and won't exclude that project from the report or the count.</p>
<p>If setup or teardown doesn't need to run as a dependency project, globalSetup and globalTeardown are the actual fix, those run outside the test hierarchy entirely so there's no test count and no report entry to filter later. But if the dependency project is needed for traces on setup, don't fight it at the config level, filter it downstream instead. Every json and blob reporter output already carries the project name on each test result, same field a dashboard or CI tool would use to separate setup noise from real counts, and a custom reporter exposes that at onTestEnd through test.parent.project()?.name.</p>
<p>playwright.config.ts:</p>
<pre><code>projects: [
  { name: 'setup', testMatch: /.*\.setup\.ts/ },
  { name: 'e2e', testMatch: /.*\.spec\.ts/, dependencies: ['setup'] },
]
</code></pre>
<p>custom-reporter.ts:</p>
<pre><code>import type { Reporter, TestCase, TestResult } from '@playwright/test/reporter';

class FilteredReporter implements Reporter {
  onTestEnd(test: TestCase, result: TestResult) {
    const projectName = test.parent.project()?.name;
    if (projectName === 'setup') return;
    // count / forward this result
  }
}

export default FilteredReporter;
</code></pre>
<p>Register it in playwright.config.ts:<br />
<code>reporter: [['./custom-reporter.ts']]</code></p>
